; ROTKPlus.lang.ini - optional, next to rotk.exe. One section per language code; keys left out use the built-in text.
; Placeholders: {label} name of the menu entry (in Teams and HeroesOnly the text it is added to, in And the names so
; far, in TeamWinner and Team the team's name), {n} a number, {hero} a hero name (in And the name added, in Team the
; players' names). TeamSun and TeamMoon are the names of the two teams of a 2 vs 2.
; Keep the texts short and, if possible, without accented letters (the menu font of the game may not have them).
; "Player" is normally taken from the game's own text; this one is used when Language is set by hand.
; The texts of the Fellowship pages can be replaced the same way, by their key: the keys are the first column of the
; table kTxt at the top of src/Players.cpp (for example PlayersMenu, PlayersStats, TabGames, StatKills). Placeholders
; there: {name}, {player}, {other}, {n}, {k}, {a}, {d}, {hero}, as in the built-in text.

